    "introductoryText": "Loads Salesforce records through the REST API, signing in with OAuth 2.0 client credentials, so a scheduled workflow runs without anyone signing in.\n\n**How to set it up**\n1. In Salesforce Setup, create or configure an **External Client App** with OAuth enabled and the **Manage user data via APIs (`api`)** scope.\n2. Enable the **Client Credentials Flow** and choose its **Run As** user in the app policies. That user's permissions decide which objects and fields the block can read: a dedicated integration user with read access to what you need is best.\n3. Copy the app's **Consumer Key** and **Consumer Secret** into the block.\n4. Enter your **My Domain URL**, such as `https://your-company.my.salesforce.com`.\n\n**Load modes**\n- **Simple - Load object** (the default): choose a common object, such as Accounts, Contacts or Opportunities. The block asks Salesforce which fields the Run As user can read and loads all of them, without SOQL or field API names.\n- **Query Builder**: an object, a list of fields, a WHERE and an ORDER BY.\n- **Custom SOQL**: any SOQL query.\n\nTwo schema actions list the objects available and describe an object's fields. Every page of results is loaded through the REST Query API.",
